2026-06-11 (Laser-Aware Selection Cut/Copy/Delete -- BUG FIX, v0.0.48): User-reported bug -- selecting a region over PART of a VOL laser and pressing Delete/Cut removed the ENTIRE laser (or, when the selection fell in a laser's middle, did nothing at all). Root cause: selCut() and selDeleteContents() in app.js treated a laser section as atomic by its start tick -- chart.lasers[s].filter(sec => !(sec.y >= lo && sec.y <= hi)) -- so a section starting inside [lo,hi] was dropped whole (even if it extended far past the selection), and a section straddling the whole selection was never touched. selCopy() had the same start-tick-only filter, so cut/copy of a partial laser lost it. (Note: selRippleDelete() already split lasers correctly with head/tail interpolation -- only the plain Delete/Cut/Copy path was wrong.) Fixed (v0.0.48): added a single DOM-free, unit-tested laser-slicing engine to chart.js as the source of truth -- ChartData.laserVAt(sec,t) (value at an absolute tick; exact for anchors/linear/step/slam, linear-approx for bezier at the cut edge), _sliceLaserSection(sec,a,b) (extracts the [a,b] sub-section with interpolated boundary anchors, preserving interior slam/interp/curve, dropping <2-point fragments), extractLaserRange(side,lo,hi) (the in-range portion rebased to lo, for the clipboard -- non-destructive) and spliceLaserRange(side,lo,hi) (removes the in-range portion IN PLACE: trims a straddling section and SPLITS a section whose middle is cut into a before-[s0,lo] and after-[hi,s1] pair). Wired all three app.js sites to the engine: selCopy -> extractLaserRange, selCut + selDeleteContents -> spliceLaserRange. Now selecting part of a laser and deleting removes only that portion and leaves the rest (with a clean interpolated edge); cutting a partial laser puts exactly that portion on the clipboard so cut->paste round-trips. Tested: 23-assertion standalone engine test (laserVAt clamp/mid/quarter, split-middle -> 2 pieces with correct boundary v, fully-inside re